<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#sourceRegion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The continental African geographic region toward which this movement, return event, or heritage relationship is oriented. Range: iroko:TraditionScheme geographic region concepts (iroko:region-west-african, iroko:region-central-african, iroko:region-east-african, iroko:region-southern-african, iroko:region-north-african, iroko:region-nile-valley). Distinct from iroko:sourceTradition, which points to a specific cultural-linguistic tradition; sourceRegion carries the broader geographic orientation when the specific tradition is not identified or when the movement is pan-regionally oriented. A Garveyite movement asserting a general Africa-wide claim would use sourceRegion rather than sourceTradition. Both properties may be asserted simultaneously."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#period-pre-1808> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#hostCommunity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The African community or institution receiving the Afro-Atlantic visitors. Range: iroko:House."@en .
