<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ReturnTypeScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Trans-Afro-Atlantic Return Types"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#return-research> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#return-research> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ReturnTypeScheme> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#paper-function-ownership-challenge> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Document contests or disrupts a claimed ownership right — through judicial petition, contested manumission, coartación claim, or challenge to the legality of original enslavement."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#corridorJurisdiction> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Atlantic trade corridor node at which this slave paper was issued, recorded, or enforced. Range: iroko:Jurisdiction (from iroko-authority.ttl). Use to link slave paper to specific port cities and colonial administrative territories in the TiSP corridor."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#type-purification> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Purification / orthodoxy movement"@en .
