<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#afroAtlanticTradition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Afro-Atlantic side of the claimed heritage relationship. Range: iroko:TraditionScheme concept."@en .
_:nf755d2f3941d4074a3cf2e3e90f6d57ab5 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-sankofa> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "1.4.1" .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#recognition-not-sought> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Not sought"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#rel-reconstructed> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The relationship is based on reconstruction from historical evidence rather than surviving living transmission."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#recognition-disputed> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Some source tradition representatives recognize the practice; others do not. Contested."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#MovementTypeScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Types de mouvement de réclamation"@fr .
