<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#sourceTradition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ReclamationMovement> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#method-cross-tradition-synthesis> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ReconstructionMethodScheme> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#type-decolonization> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Décolonisation"@fr .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#slavePaperType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#SlavePaper> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#paper-type-irregular-forged> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A document in the slave paper chain that was fraudulently produced, backdated, altered, or otherwise irregular. Analytically essential for the post-1820 period of illegal trade: the prevalence of forged documentation reveals the legal requirements of the official system and the networks that circumvented them."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#method-oral-tradition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Reconstruction based on oral transmission from living elders or communities with partial survival of the tradition."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#HeritageRelationshipTypeScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Types de relation patrimoniale"@fr .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#paper-type-official-correspondence> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Letters, reports, or memoranda between colonial administrators, customs officials, port authorities, or clergy concerning the movement, legal status, or trade of enslaved persons. Includes instructions on trade suppression enforcement in the post-1808 period."@en .
